{"duration_api_ms": 85820, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "3c45dedb-b8ad-46ad-8b72-013b51fe2671", "total_cost_usd": 0.16411769999999998, "usage": {"input_tokens": 226, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 28555, "cache_read_input_tokens": 739017, "output_tokens": 6576, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 962}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 28555, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 8, "output_tokens": 1097, "cache_read_input_tokens": 40128, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 380, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 380}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "modelUsage": {"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001": {"inputTokens": 226, "outputTokens": 6576, "cacheReadInputTokens": 739017, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 28555, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.16411769999999998, "contextWindow": 200000, "maxOutputTokens": 32000, "thinkingTokens": 962, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-4-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 28, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "## Summary\n\nI've read through the SPEC and codebase. Here's what an implementer needs to know to complete the five missing commands:\n\n### The Three Export Systems\n\n**System A (Ardent)** — ISO dates in dollars\n- Format: Comment banner, header, CSV data\n- Columns: `entry_id, posted_on (YYYY-MM-DD), account, memo, amount ($), currency`\n- Amounts are dollars with 2 decimals; negative = refund\n\n**System B (Borough)** — ISO dates in cents\n- Format: Just header + CSV data (no banner)\n- Columns: `sys (always \"B\"), doc_no, value_date (YYYY-MM-DD), acct, descr, amount (cents!), cur`\n- **Critical**: amounts are in whole cents, not dollars—divide by 100\n- No field quoting; descriptions already sanitized\n\n**System C (Calder)** — Day-first dates in dollars\n- Format: Banner, header, CSV data, trailer (`== N rows ==`)\n- Columns: `ref, txn_date (DD/MM/YYYY!), ledger_acct, narrative, gross_amount ($), ccy`\n- Amounts are dollars; **dates must be parsed as dd/mm/yyyy**, not mm/dd/yyyy\n\n### What Must Be Normalized\n\nAll systems produce Records with exactly this header and order:\n```\nrecord_id,source_system,date,account_code,account_name,description,amount\n```\n\nEvery unknown account code gets the label from `[report] unknown_account_label` setting instead of being blank. Rows come out sorted by: date (ISO format), system letter (A/B/C), record_id.\n\n### The Five Commands\n\n**1. ingest** — Merge any mix of exports into one CSV\n- Input: Multiple files from any systems, any order\n- Output: CSV to `--out` (default `out/records.csv`); creates parent dirs\n- After success, print `wrote=<count> to <path>` to stdout\n\n**2. report** — Totals by account or month\n- `--by account` → account_code ascending, shows each account's total\n- `--by month` → YYYY-MM ascending, shows each month's total\n- Totals use **half-to-even rounding** (Decimal's default, not ROUND_HALF_UP)\n- Decimals shown per `[report] decimals` setting\n- Refunds excluded by default; use `--include-refunds` to include them\n\n**3. reconcile** — Find disagreements between systems\n- Group by account+month+system, sum each group\n- Report combinations where 2+ systems posted and their spread (max−min) exceeds tolerance\n- Tolerance defaults to `[reconcile] tolerance` setting; override with `--tolerance N`\n- Print mismatches ordered by account then month: `MISMATCH 4200 2026-02 spread=57.75 A=455.00 B=512.75 C=-`\n- End with `mismatches=<n>`\n\n**4. validate** — Reject malformed rows\n- Check field count matches header\n- Parse each date in the format that system writes\n- Parse amount as a number\n- Match account code against `[validate] account_code_pattern` (default `^[0-9]{4}$`)\n- Log warnings to stderr, print `checked=<total> rejected=<bad>` to stdout\n- Exit 2 if any rejected, 0 if all pass\n\n**5. --config PATH** — Global flag (before subcommand)\n- Override settings file for one run (don't edit checked-in `config/settings.toml`)\n- Settings layer: defaults → config/settings.toml → LEDGERKIT_CONFIG env var → `--config` arg\n\n### Key Technical Constraints\n\n- **Amounts**: Always `decimal.Decimal`, never `float`. Convert cents to dollars in the reader.\n- **Dates**: `datetime.date` objects. System A/B are ISO; System C is dd/mm/yyyy.\n- **Rounding**: Half to even (Decimal's default quantize mode), not half up.\n- **Logging**: Use `from ledgerkit.log import get_logger; _log = get_logger(__name__)` for warnings about data.\n- **Output**: Only `ledgerkit.cli.emit()` prints to stdout; everything else uses the logger.\n- **No new dependencies**, no utils.cache, no legacy_parser, full type annotations on all public functions.", "ttft_ms": 1855, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 87990, "uuid": "698ab296-ee9b-4326-8da7-f465d9f0ae1a", "ttft_stream_ms": 949, "time_to_request_ms": 137, "first_content_frame_ms": 1183, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-1-task", "_wall_s": 89.5, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0